    {
      "id": "the-count-of-monte-cristo-s005-p00530",
      "source_en": "\"So far, then,\" said Danglars, mentally, \"all has gone as I would have it. I am, temporarily, commander of the Pharaon, with the certainty of being permanently so, if that fool of a Caderousse can be persuaded to hold his tongue. My only fear is the chance of Dantes being released. But, there, he is in the hands of Justice; and,\" added he with a smile, \"she will take her own.\" So saying, he leaped into a boat, desiring to be rowed on board the Pharaon, where M. Morrel had agreed to meet him.",
